        "hypothesis": "The starting skill preserves basic legal-hold and approval behavior but still applies the old seven-day threshold and omits r2 validation, export protection, category thresholds, and approval validity. Replacing that rule with ordered, strict r2 conditions should correct the observed policy failures while preserving classification-only behavior, legal-hold precedence, approved eligible deletion, and keeping younger records.",
        "proposal": "main/13e07541eaab24c6bd2d9fc528a575adaa40c15bdd62e189e7afe46c7235ca13/retention-migration/0/proposal/0",
        "status": "accept",
        "files": {
          "SKILL.md": "---\nname: synthetic-retention\ndescription: Classify a fictional record under retention policy r2.\n---\n\n# Synthetic Retention\n\nClassify each record independently under policy r2. Return JSON only. For an individual record, return one object with an `action` field whose value is `keep`, `delete`, or `review`. When a batch request specifies an ID-to-action mapping, use that requested JSON mapping.\n\nIf the input supplies defaults, merge them with each record before classification. Explicit record values, including null, override defaults. Do not invent missing values or coerce types. Exactly true means the JSON boolean true; missing flags, strings, numbers, and null are not true. A valid number means a finite, nonnegative JSON number; numeric strings, booleans, null, and missing values are invalid.\n\nEvaluate these rules in order and stop at the first decision:\n\n1. If `legalHold` is exactly true, choose `keep`, regardless of all other fields.\n2. Otherwise, if `pendingExport` is exactly true, choose `keep`, regardless of all remaining fields.\n3. Otherwise, require a valid number for `age` and a `category` exactly equal to `audit`, `operational`, or `ephemeral`. If either requirement fails, choose `review`.\n4. The eligibility threshold is 90 days for `audit`, 30 days for `operational`, and 7 days for `ephemeral`. If `age` is below the applicable threshold, choose `keep`, regardless of approval or owner fields. Equality with the threshold is eligible.\n5. For an eligible record, choose `delete` only if all of the following hold: `ownerVerified` is exactly true; `approval` is exactly true; `approvalPolicy` is exactly the string `r2`; both `now` and `approvalExpiresAt` are valid numbers; and `approvalExpiresAt` is greater than or equal to `now`. Otherwise choose `review`.\n\nApply these conditions to every record without ID-specific exceptions. Classify only; do not delete anything, perform retention operations, or use tools.\n"
        }
      }
    ]
